            <abstract>
                <para>Our research and restoration programme focuses on the region’s unique, biologically diverse tropical rainforests in the Western Ghats, with a specific focus on the Anamalai Hills.

This dataset focuses on 11 threatened tree species and other plant species recorded during the surveys.</para>
            </abstract>
            <funding>
                <para>The threatened trees surveys and compilation and publication of this dataset was supported by Fondation Franklinia. The project was also supported by Rohini Nilekani Philanthropies and Rainmatter Foundation.</para>
            </funding>
            <studyAreaDescription>
                <descriptor name="generic"
                            citableClassificationSystem="false">
                    <descriptorValue>The study was carried out within the Anamalai Tiger Reserve (ATR), Tamil Nadu, India (core zone: 958 km², (10°22&apos; - 10°56&apos;N, 76°815&apos; - 77°418&apos;E) and the adjoining Valparai Plateau (220 km², 10°24- 10°46&apos;N, 76°82&apos; - 77°05&apos;E) in the Anamalai Hills of the Western Ghats. Field surveys were carried out in some rainforest fragments on the Valparai Plateau and rainforest tracts in ATR.</descriptorValue>
                </descriptor>
